{"cmd": "cd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_002/workspace && mkdir -p scripts && cat > scripts/call.py <<'EOF'\nimport csv, glob, os\nABX=[l.strip() for l in open('data/antibiotics.txt') if l.strip()]\n# rules: gene-symbol prefixes / exact symbols -> antibiotic\nAMP=('blaTEM','blaSHV','blaCTX-M','blaOXA-1','blaOXA-10','blaOXA-48','blaNDM','blaKPC','blaVIM','blaIMP','blaCMY','blaDHA','blaOXA-')\nESBL=('blaCTX-M','blaSHV-12','blaCMY','blaDHA','blaNDM','blaKPC','blaVIM','blaIMP')\nCARB=('blaNDM','blaKPC','blaVIM','blaIMP','blaOXA-48','blaOXA-181','blaOXA-232','blaOXA-244')\nGEN=('aac(3)-II','aac(3)-IV','aac(3)-VI','aac(3)-I','ant(2'')-Ia','armA','rmtB','rmtC','npmA')\nQRDR=('gyrA_','parC_','parE_S458')\ndef hits(f):\n    r=list(csv.DictReader(open(f),delimiter='\\t'))\n    return [x for x in r if x['Type']=='AMR' and x['Scope']=='core']\nout=open('output/predictions.tsv','w')\nout.write('isolate_id\\tantibiotic\\tprediction\\tevidence\\n')\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('output/amrfinder/ISO_*.tsv')):\n    iso=os.path.basename(f)[:-4]; h=hits(f); s=[x['Element symbol'] for x in h]\n    def tag(x): return x['Element symbol']+('' if x['Method'] in('EXACTX','ALLELEX','POINTX') else f\"({x['Method']},cov{x['% Coverage of reference']})\")\n    def find(pred): return [tag(x) for x in h if pred(x['Element symbol'])]\n    for a in ABX:\n        if a=='ampicillin': e=find(lambda g:g.startswith(AMP)); \n        elif a=='cefotaxime': e=find(lambda g:g.startswith(ESBL))\n        elif a=='meropenem': e=find(lambda g:g.startswith(CARB))\n        elif a=='gentamicin': e=find(lambda g:g.startswith(GEN))\n        elif a=='ciprofloxacin':\n            e=find(lambda g:g.startswith(QRDR) or g.startswith(('qnr','aac(6\\')-Ib-cr','qepA','oqx')))\n        elif a.startswith('trimethoprim'): e=find(lambda g:g.startswith('dfr'))\n        call='R' if e else 'S'; ev='; '.join(e) if e else 'no determinant found'\n        if a=='ciprofloxacin' and e: \n            ev+='; ' + ('single low-level determinant, borderline MIC' if len(e)==1 else 'multiple QRDR/PMQR determinants')\n        if a.startswith('trimethoprim') and e:\n            su=find(lambda g:g.startswith('sul')); ev+=('; '+'; '.join(su)) if su else '; no sul gene (dfr alone)'\n        if a=='cefotaxime' and not e:\n            o=find(lambda g:g.startswith(('blaOXA-10','blaOXA-48','blaTEM-1')))\n            if o: ev='only narrow-spectrum/non-ESBL beta-lactamase: '+'; '.join(o)\n        if a=='meropenem' and 'blaOXA-48' in s: ev+='; OXA-48 may give low-level MIC near breakpoint'\n        out.write(f'{iso}\\t{a}\\t{call}\\t{ev}\\n')\nEOF\npython3 -I scripts/call.py && column -t -s$'\\t' output/predictions.tsv", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "isolate_id  antibiotic                     prediction  evidence\nISO_011     ampicillin                     R           blaOXA-10; blaTEM-1\nISO_011     cefotaxime                     S           only narrow-spectrum/non-ESBL beta-lactamase: blaOXA-10; blaTEM-1\nISO_011     ciprofloxacin                  R           qnrS1; gyrA_S83L; multiple QRDR/PMQR determinants\nISO_011     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_011     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_011     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA14; sul3\nISO_012     ampicillin                     R           blaOXA-48\nISO_012     cefotaxime                     S           only narrow-spectrum/non-ESBL beta-lactamase: blaOXA-48\nISO_012     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_012     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_012     meropenem                      R           blaOXA-48; OXA-48 may give low-level MIC near breakpoint\nISO_012     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_013     ampicillin                     R           blaNDM-5; blaCTX-M-14; blaTEM-1\nISO_013     cefotaxime                     R           blaNDM-5; blaCTX-M-14\nISO_013     ciprofloxacin                  R           parC_S80I; parE_S458A; gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; multiple QRDR/PMQR determinants\nISO_013     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IVa\nISO_013     meropenem                      R           blaNDM-5\nISO_013     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA12; sul2\nISO_014     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_014     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_014     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_014     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_014     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_014     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_015     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_015     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_015     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_015     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_015     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_015     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_016     ampicillin                     R           blaSHV-12; blaTEM-1\nISO_016     cefotaxime                     R           blaSHV-12\nISO_016     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_S83L; single low-level determinant, borderline MIC\nISO_016     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_016     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_016     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA1; no sul gene (dfr alone)\nISO_017     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM(BLASTX,cov97.90)\nISO_017     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_017     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_017     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IId(PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX,cov86.71)\nISO_017     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_017     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; sul2; sul1\nISO_018     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-55; blaOXA-10\nISO_018     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-55\nISO_018     ciprofloxacin                  R           qnrS1; single low-level determinant, borderline MIC\nISO_018     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_018     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_018     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA14; no sul gene (dfr alone)\nISO_019     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_019     cefotaxime                     S           only narrow-spectrum/non-ESBL beta-lactamase: blaTEM-1\nISO_019     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_019     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_019     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_019     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA1; sul1\nISO_020     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_020     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_020     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_020     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_020     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_020     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01ADCG8Zm3fiCRwYPaekF4hU", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_002"}
{"cmd": "cat > output/methods.md <<'EOF'\n# Methods\n\n## Tools and databases\n- **AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7** (`amrfinder`), database version **2026-10-29.1**\n  (`.../envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`). This was the only dedicated AMR caller\n  installed. abricate, RGI, ResFinder, staramr and mlst were not present.\n- BLAST+ 2.17.0 and HMMER, used internally by AMRFinderPlus.\n- Python 3 for the genotype-to-phenotype rules (`scripts/call.py`, kept in the workspace).\n\n## Command (per isolate)\n```\namrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta -O Escherichia --plus --threads 4 --name ISO_### -o output/amrfinder/ISO_###.tsv\n```\n`-O Escherichia` turns on species-specific point-mutation screening (gyrA/parC/parE, ampC promoter,\nporins, etc.) and filters out intrinsic genes. `--plus` adds stress, virulence and efflux genes,\nwhich were not used for the calls. Default identity and coverage thresholds were kept. Raw output is in\n`output/amrfinder/`.\n\n## Genotype-to-phenotype rules\nOnly `Scope = core`, `Type = AMR` elements were used. Partial or contig-edge hits (PARTIALX,\nPARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX, BLASTX) were accepted and labelled in the evidence column. An isolate was\ncalled **R** if any of the listed determinants was found, otherwise **S**. No call was NA.\n\n| Antibiotic | Determinants that give R |\n|---|---|\n| ampicillin | any acquired beta-lactamase (blaTEM, blaSHV, blaCTX-M, blaOXA incl. OXA-10/OXA-48, blaNDM, blaKPC, blaVIM, blaIMP, plasmid AmpC CMY/DHA) |\n| cefotaxime | ESBL / plasmid AmpC / MBL / KPC (blaCTX-M, blaSHV-12, blaCMY, blaDHA, blaNDM, blaKPC, blaVIM, blaIMP). blaTEM-1, blaOXA-10 and blaOXA-48 alone were treated as not giving cefotaxime R. Chromosomal blaEC (intrinsic, `plus` scope) was ignored because no ampC promoter mutation was reported. |\n| meropenem | carbapenemase (blaNDM, blaKPC, blaVIM, blaIMP, blaOXA-48-like). OXA-48 was called R, though it can give MICs near the breakpoint. |\n| gentamicin | aac(3)-II/-IV/-VI family, ant(2'')-Ia, 16S rRNA methylases (armA, rmt*, npmA). aadA, aph(3'), aph(3'') and aph(6) were not counted. |\n| ciprofloxacin | any QRDR mutation reported by AMRFinderPlus in gyrA or parC, or parE S458, or any PMQR gene (qnr, aac(6')-Ib-cr, qepA, oqxAB). parE I355T (ISO_020) was not counted. A single determinant (gyrA S83L alone, or qnrS1 alone) was called R but flagged as borderline. marR/acrR substitutions were not counted. |\n| trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole | any acquired dfrA gene, with or without sul1/2/3. A sul gene alone was not enough. |\n\n## Caveats\n- Calls are presence/absence only. Expression levels, copy number and porin/efflux contributions were not modelled.\n- Borderline calls: ciprofloxacin for ISO_016 (gyrA S83L only) and ISO_018 (qnrS1 only);\n  meropenem for ISO_012 (OXA-48 alone); cefotaxime for ISO_011 and ISO_012 (OXA-10 / OXA-48, called S).\nEOF\nawk -F'\\t' 'NR>1' output/predictions.tsv | wc -l", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "      60", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01NZ4DcWYA6R8EH7oVoZY7TC", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_002"}
