{"cmd": "cd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_005/workspace; mkdir -p scripts; cat > scripts/call.py <<'EOF'\nimport csv, glob, os, re\nabx=[l.strip() for l in open('data/antibiotics.txt') if l.strip()]\nout=open('output/predictions.tsv','w'); out.write('isolate_id\\tantibiotic\\tprediction\\tevidence\\n')\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('output/amrfinder/*.tsv')):\n    iso=os.path.basename(f)[:-4]\n    rows=[r for r in csv.DictReader(open(f),delimiter='\\t') if r['Type']=='AMR']\n    g=[r['Element symbol'] for r in rows if r['Method'] not in ('PARTIALX','PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX','INTERNAL_STOP')]\n    def m(p): return [x for x in g if re.match(p,x)]\n    for a in abx:\n        if a=='ampicillin':\n            d=m(r'bla(TEM|SHV|CTX-M|OXA|CMY|DHA|ACT|NDM|KPC|VIM|IMP|PSE|CARB)'); call='R' if d else 'S'\n        elif a=='cefotaxime':\n            d=m(r'bla(CTX-M|CMY|DHA|ACT|NDM|KPC|VIM|IMP|OXA-48|SHV-(2|5|12))')+m(r'blaEC-|ampC_')\n            call='R' if d else 'S'\n        elif a=='ciprofloxacin':\n            gy=m(r'gyrA_'); pc=m(r'par[CE]_'); q=m(r'qnr|aac\\(6\\'\\)-Ib-cr|qep|oqx')\n            d=gy+pc+q\n            call='R' if (len(gy)>=2 or (gy and pc) or (gy and q)) else ('S' if not (gy or q) else 'R' if (gy and q) else 'S')\n            if not (len(gy)>=2 or (gy and (pc or q))): d=d if d else []\n            if call=='S' and d: d=d+['(insufficient for R: needs >=2 QRDR changes or gyrA+PMQR)']\n        elif a=='gentamicin':\n            d=m(r'aac\\(3\\)-(I|II|III|IV|VI)|ant\\(2\\'\\'\\)|armA|rmt|npmA|aac\\(6\\'\\)-Ib\\'?$'); d=[x for x in d if not x.startswith(\"aac(6')-Ib\")] ; call='R' if d else 'S'\n        elif a=='meropenem':\n            d=m(r'bla(KPC|NDM|VIM|IMP|OXA-48|OXA-181|OXA-232|OXA-244|GES-5)'); call='R' if d else 'S'\n        elif a=='trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole':\n            dfr=m(r'dfr'); sul=m(r'sul[123]'); d=dfr+sul; call='R' if (dfr and sul) else 'S'\n            if call=='S' and d: d=d+['(only one of dfr/sul present)']\n        else:\n            d=[];call='NA'\n        ev=', '.join(d) if d else 'no determinant found'\n        out.write(f'{iso}\\t{a}\\t{call}\\t{ev}\\n')\nEOF\npython3 -I scripts/call.py; column -t -s$'\\t' output/predictions.tsv | cut -c1-140", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "isolate_id  antibiotic                     prediction  evidence\nISO_041     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1, blaCTX-M-15, blaOXA-1\nISO_041     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-15\nISO_041     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N, gyrA_S83L, parE_S458A, parC_S80I, aac(6')-Ib-cr5\nISO_041     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IIe\nISO_041     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_041     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17, sul1\nISO_042     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-65\nISO_042     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-65\nISO_042     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87Y, gyrA_S83L, parE_S458A, parC_S80I\nISO_042     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IVa\nISO_042     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_042     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA12, sul2\nISO_043     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_043     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_043     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_043     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_043     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_043     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA5, sul1\nISO_044     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_044     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_044     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_044     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_044     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_044     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_045     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_045     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_045     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_045     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_045     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_045     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_046     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_046     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_046     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N, gyrA_S83L, parC_S57T, parC_S80I, parE_S458A\nISO_046     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_046     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_046     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17, sul1\nISO_047     ampicillin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_047     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_047     ciprofloxacin                  S           no determinant found\nISO_047     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_047     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_047     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no determinant found\nISO_048     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1, blaCMY-2\nISO_048     cefotaxime                     R           blaCMY-2\nISO_048     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N, gyrA_S83L, parE_S458A, parC_S80I, qnrS1\nISO_048     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IId\nISO_048     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_048     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA12, sul2, sul1\nISO_049     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-1, blaTEM-1\nISO_049     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-1\nISO_049     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N, gyrA_S83L, parC_A56T, parC_S80I\nISO_049     gentamicin                     S           no determinant found\nISO_049     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_049     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17, sul1, sul2\nISO_050     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_050     cefotaxime                     S           no determinant found\nISO_050     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N, gyrA_S83L, parC_S80I, parE_L445H\nISO_050     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IId\nISO_050     meropenem                      S           no determinant found\nISO_050     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17, sul2, sul1", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01LoucXFTzLXJcjCv8QryLhJ", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_005"}
{"cmd": "cd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_005/workspace; cat > output/methods.md <<'EOF'\n# Methods\n\n## Tools and databases\n- **AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7** (`amrfinder`, conda env `amr`), database version **2026-10-29.1**\n  (`.../envs/amr/share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`). Versions checked with `amrfinder -V`.\n- BLAST+ 2.17.0 (used internally by AMRFinderPlus).\n- Python 3 (standard library only) for genotype-to-phenotype translation (`scripts/call.py`).\n- No other AMR tools (ResFinder/PointFinder, RGI, ABRicate, staramr) were installed. No internet access was used.\n\n## Command (per isolate)\n```\namrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta -O Escherichia --plus --threads 4 --name ISO_### -o output/amrfinder/ISO_###.tsv\n```\n`-O Escherichia` enables species-specific point-mutation screening (gyrA, parC, parE, ampC promoter, etc.)\nand suppresses intrinsic-gene noise; `--plus` reports additional (efflux/stress) elements. Default\nidentity/coverage thresholds were used. Raw outputs are in `output/amrfinder/`.\n\n## Genotype -> S/R rules\nOnly `Type == AMR` rows were used. Hits with method PARTIALX / PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX / INTERNAL_STOP were\nexcluded (none of these affected a call: catB3, aadA1, aadA2 only). Chromosomal blaEC (intrinsic ampC) was\nignored unless a promoter/attenuator mutation was reported (none were). Efflux genes (acrF, mdtM, emrD) and\nregulatory mutations (marR, acrR, soxS) were not counted as sufficient for resistance.\n\n| Antibiotic | R if any of |\n|---|---|\n| ampicillin | acquired beta-lactamase: blaTEM, blaSHV, blaCTX-M, blaOXA, blaCMY, blaDHA, blaACT, carbapenemases, etc. |\n| cefotaxime | ESBL or AmpC: blaCTX-M, ESBL-type SHV, plasmid AmpC (blaCMY/DHA/ACT), carbapenemases, or ampC promoter mutation. blaTEM-1 and blaOXA-1 alone -> S |\n| ciprofloxacin | >=2 QRDR mutations in gyrA, or gyrA mutation + parC/parE mutation, or gyrA mutation + PMQR gene (qnr, aac(6')-Ib-cr, qepA, oqxAB). A single change or marR/acrR/soxS alone -> S |\n| gentamicin | aac(3)-I/II/III/IV/VI variants, ant(2'')-Ia, or 16S rRNA methylases (armA, rmt*, npmA). aac(6')-Ib(-cr) not counted |\n| meropenem | carbapenemase (KPC, NDM, VIM, IMP, OXA-48-like, GES-5). Porin loss (e.g. ompF_W83Ter in ISO_042) not counted alone |\n| trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole | at least one dfr gene AND at least one sul gene (sul1/2/3); only one of the two -> S |\n\nNo call was NA. The `evidence` column lists the AMRFinderPlus element symbols that drove each call\n(for ciprofloxacin, all QRDR mutations and PMQR genes found).\nEOF\nwc -l output/predictions.tsv", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "      61 output/predictions.tsv", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01QynCyqJbZc5eJkhpSSpCfv", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_005"}
