{"cmd": "mkdir -p /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_008/workspace/output/scripts; cat > /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_008/workspace/output/scripts/call.py <<'EOF'\nimport csv, glob, os, re, sys\nws = sys.argv[1]\nabx = [l.strip() for l in open(os.path.join(ws, \"data/antibiotics.txt\")) if l.strip()]\ndef hits(iso):\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(open(os.path.join(ws, f\"output/amrfinder/{iso}.tsv\")), delimiter=\"\\t\"))\n    return [r for r in rows if r[\"Type\"] == \"AMR\"]\nCARB = re.compile(r\"^bla(KPC|NDM|VIM|IMP|OXA-48|OXA-181|OXA-232|OXA-244|OXA-162|OXA-204|OXA-23|GES-5|SME|IMI|NMC)\")\nESBL_AMPC = re.compile(r\"^bla(CTX-M|SHV-(?!1$|11$)|TEM-(?!1$|2$)|CMY|DHA|ACC|FOX|MOX|ACT|MIR|PER|VEB|GES|BEL|KPC|NDM|VIM|IMP)\")\nGENT = re.compile(r\"^(aac\\(3\\)|ant\\(2''\\)|aac\\(6'\\)-Ib'?|rmt|armA|npmA)\")\ndef call(iso, ab, H):\n    syms = [h[\"Element symbol\"] for h in H]\n    acq_bla = [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"bla\") and s != \"blaEC\"]\n    if ab == \"ampicillin\":\n        ev = acq_bla + [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"ampC_\")]\n        return (\"R\", \"; \".join(ev)) if ev else (\"S\", \"no acquired beta-lactamase; chromosomal blaEC only\")\n    if ab == \"cefotaxime\":\n        ev = [s for s in acq_bla if ESBL_AMPC.match(s)] + [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"blaEC\") and h_sub(H, s, \"CEPHALOSPORIN\")]\n        ev = [s for s in acq_bla if ESBL_AMPC.match(s)]\n        return (\"R\", \"; \".join(ev)) if ev else (\"S\", \"no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\" + (f\" ({'; '.join(acq_bla)} present, narrow-spectrum)\" if acq_bla else \"\"))\n    if ab == \"ciprofloxacin\":\n        gyr = [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"gyrA_\")]\n        par = [s for s in syms if s.startswith((\"parC_\", \"parE_\"))]\n        pmqr = [s for s in syms if s.startswith((\"qnr\", \"aac(6')-Ib-cr\", \"qepA\", \"oqx\"))]\n        ev = gyr + par + pmqr\n        if gyr and (len(gyr) + len([p for p in par if p.startswith(\"parC\")]) + len(pmqr)) >= 2:\n            return \"R\", \"; \".join(ev)\n        if gyr or (pmqr and par):\n            return \"R\", \"; \".join(ev)\n        return (\"S\", \"no QRDR mutation\" + (f\"; {'; '.join(ev)} only\" if ev else \"\")) \n    if ab == \"gentamicin\":\n        ev = [s for s in syms if GENT.match(s) and not s.startswith(\"aac(6')-Ib\")]\n        return (\"R\", \"; \".join(ev)) if ev else (\"S\", \"no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\")\n    if ab == \"meropenem\":\n        ev = [s for s in acq_bla if CARB.match(s)]\n        if ev: return \"R\", \"; \".join(ev)\n        por = [s for s in syms if s.startswith((\"ompC_\", \"ompF_\"))]\n        return \"S\", \"no carbapenemase\" + (f\" ({'; '.join(por)} noted, insufficient alone)\" if por else \"\")\n    if ab == \"trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\":\n        dfr = [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"dfr\")]\n        sul = [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"sul\")]\n        if dfr: return \"R\", \"; \".join(dfr + sul)\n        return \"S\", \"no dfr gene\" + (f\" ({'; '.join(sul)} only)\" if sul else \"\")\n    return \"NA\", \"antibiotic not covered by rules\"\ndef h_sub(H, s, sub): return False\nout = open(os.path.join(ws, \"output/predictions.tsv\"), \"w\")\nout.write(\"isolate_id\\tantibiotic\\tprediction\\tevidence\\n\")\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(ws, \"data/genomes/*.fasta\"))):\n    iso = os.path.basename(f)[:-6]\n    H = hits(iso)\n    for ab in abx:\n        p, e = call(iso, ab, H)\n        out.write(f\"{iso}\\t{ab}\\t{p}\\t{e}\\n\")\nEOF\ncd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_008/workspace && python3 -I output/scripts/call.py \"$PWD\" && python3 --version && column -t -s$'\\t' output/predictions.tsv", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "Python 3.13.13\nisolate_id  antibiotic                     prediction  evidence\nISO_071     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M; ampC_T-32A\nISO_071     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M\nISO_071     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; parC_E84V; parC_S80I; parE_I529L\nISO_071     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_071     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_071     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no dfr gene\nISO_072     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-15; blaOXA-1\nISO_072     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-15\nISO_072     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; parC_E84V; parC_S80I; parE_I529L; aac(6')-Ib-cr5\nISO_072     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_072     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_072     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; sul1\nISO_073     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-1\nISO_073     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-1\nISO_073     ciprofloxacin                  S           no QRDR mutation\nISO_073     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_073     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_073     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no dfr gene (sul1; sul2 only)\nISO_074     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1; blaOXA-48\nISO_074     cefotaxime                     S           no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase (blaTEM-1; blaOXA-48 present, narrow-spectrum)\nISO_074     ciprofloxacin                  S           no QRDR mutation\nISO_074     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_074     meropenem                      R           blaOXA-48\nISO_074     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA5; sul2\nISO_075     ampicillin                     R           blaOXA-1; blaKPC-3\nISO_075     cefotaxime                     R           blaKPC-3\nISO_075     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; parE_I529L; parC_E84V; parC_S80I; aac(6')-Ib-cr5\nISO_075     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_075     meropenem                      R           blaKPC-3\nISO_075     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; sul1\nISO_076     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_076     cefotaxime                     S           no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase (blaTEM-1 present, narrow-spectrum)\nISO_076     ciprofloxacin                  S           no QRDR mutation\nISO_076     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_076     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_076     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA8; sul2\nISO_077     ampicillin                     S           no acquired beta-lactamase; chromosomal blaEC only\nISO_077     cefotaxime                     S           no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\nISO_077     ciprofloxacin                  S           no QRDR mutation\nISO_077     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_077     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_077     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  S           no dfr gene\nISO_078     ampicillin                     R           blaCTX-M-55; blaTEM\nISO_078     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-55\nISO_078     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; parC_S80I; parE_S458A\nISO_078     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IId; rmtB1\nISO_078     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_078     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; dfrA12; sul1; sul3\nISO_079     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1\nISO_079     cefotaxime                     S           no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase (blaTEM-1 present, narrow-spectrum)\nISO_079     ciprofloxacin                  S           no QRDR mutation\nISO_079     gentamicin                     S           no gentamicin-modifying enzyme or 16S methylase\nISO_079     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase\nISO_079     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; sul1\nISO_080     ampicillin                     R           blaTEM-1; blaCTX-M-15; blaOXA-1\nISO_080     cefotaxime                     R           blaCTX-M-15\nISO_080     ciprofloxacin                  R           gyrA_D87N; gyrA_S83L; parE_S458A; parC_S80I; aac(6')-Ib-cr5\nISO_080     gentamicin                     R           aac(3)-IId\nISO_080     meropenem                      S           no carbapenemase (ompF_Y253EfsTer3 noted, insufficient alone)\nISO_080     trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole  R           dfrA17; sul1", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01LxW3aperty59JQVw1qhS6G", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_008"}
{"cmd": "python3 - <<'EOF'\np=\"output/scripts/call.py\"; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('''        ev = [s for s in acq_bla if ESBL_AMPC.match(s)] + [s for s in syms if s.startswith(\"blaEC\") and h_sub(H, s, \"CEPHALOSPORIN\")]\\n''','')\ns=s.replace('def h_sub(H, s, sub): return False\\n','')\ns=s.replace('''\"no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\" + (f\" ({'; '.join(acq_bla)} present, narrow-spectrum)\"''','''\"no ESBL/plasmid AmpC/KPC-type enzyme\" + (f\" ({'; '.join(acq_bla)} present; poor cefotaxime hydrolysis)\"''')\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -I output/scripts/call.py \"$PWD\" && grep cefotaxime output/predictions.tsv | grep -c . && wc -l output/predictions.tsv && grep ISO_074.*cefo output/predictions.tsv", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "10\n      61 output/predictions.tsv\n(eval):8: no matches found: ISO_074.*cefo", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_014yibbS67E5zxW5y6xkWU2g", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_008"}
{"cmd": "grep 'ISO_074' output/predictions.tsv | grep cefo; cat > output/methods.md <<'EOF'\n# Methods\n\n## Tools and versions\n- **AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7** (`amrfinder`), database version **2026-10-29.1**\n  (`.../share/amrfinderplus/data/2026-10-29.1`), with its bundled BLAST+ **2.17.0+** (blastn/tblastn) and stxtyper.\n- Python 3.13.13 for the genotype-to-phenotype rules (`output/scripts/call.py`).\n- Other tools checked but not installed: abricate, RGI, ResFinder/PointFinder, ARIBA, staramr, mlst.\n  Nothing was downloaded.\n\n## Command (per isolate)\n```\namrfinder -n data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta -O Escherichia --plus --threads 4 -o output/amrfinder/ISO_###.tsv\n```\nDefaults kept: identity/coverage thresholds from the curated database (`-i`/`-c` not set).\n`-O Escherichia` turns on chromosomal point-mutation screening (gyrA, parC, parE, ampC promoter, porins, ftsI, etc.).\nThe raw reports are in `output/amrfinder/`.\n\n## Genotype → phenotype rules\nThese rules use only rows of type `AMR`. Partial hits (PARTIAL/PARTIAL_CONTIG_END) were counted as present.\nThe chromosomal `blaEC` (intrinsic *E. coli* AmpC) was ignored.\n\n| Antibiotic | R if |\n|---|---|\n| ampicillin | any acquired beta-lactamase (`bla*` other than blaEC: TEM, OXA-1, CTX-M, OXA-48, KPC, ...) or an ampC promoter mutation |\n| cefotaxime | an ESBL, a plasmid AmpC, or a cefotaximase carbapenemase: CTX-M, non-TEM-1/2 TEM, non-SHV-1/11 SHV, CMY/DHA/ACC/FOX/MOX/ACT/MIR, PER/VEB/GES, KPC/NDM/VIM/IMP. Called S when only TEM-1, OXA-1 or OXA-48 is present (OXA-48 hydrolyses cefotaxime poorly) |\n| ciprofloxacin | any gyrA QRDR mutation (all R calls here had gyrA S83L+D87N plus parC S80I, i.e. high-level), or a PMQR gene (qnr, aac(6')-Ib-cr, qepA) together with a parC/parE mutation |\n| gentamicin | aac(3)-*, ant(2'')-Ia, or a 16S rRNA methylase (rmt*, armA, npmA). aac(6')-Ib(-cr) does not count |\n| meropenem | an acquired carbapenemase (KPC, NDM, VIM, IMP, OXA-48-like, ...). A porin defect alone (ompF/ompC) was noted in the evidence but called S |\n| trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole | any acquired `dfr` gene (sul genes are listed as supporting evidence; sul without dfr is called S) |\n\nIf no rule fires, the call is S with \"no determinant found\"-type evidence. No NA calls were needed.\n\n## Caveats\n- OXA-48 → meropenem R is a conservative call. OXA-48 producers often have meropenem MICs near or below the clinical breakpoint.\n- ISO_080 has an ompF frameshift with CTX-M-15 + OXA-1 and was called meropenem S. Ertapenem would be more affected than meropenem.\n- Gene expression, copy number and MIC breakpoints were not modelled.\nEOF\nls output", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "ISO_074\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/plasmid AmpC/KPC-type enzyme (blaTEM-1; blaOXA-48 present; poor cefotaxime hydrolysis)\namrfinder\nmethods.md\npredictions.tsv\nscripts", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01EqGMHWMTESTFTz9pg2nzwY", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_008"}
