{"cmd": "cd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_010/workspace; mkdir -p scripts; cat > scripts/call.py <<'EOF'\nimport csv, glob, os, re, sys\nabx = [l.strip() for l in open('data/antibiotics.txt') if l.strip()]\nout = open('output/predictions.tsv','w')\nout.write('isolate_id\\tantibiotic\\tprediction\\tevidence\\n')\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('output/amrfinder/ISO_*.tsv')):\n    iso = os.path.basename(f)[:-4]\n    rows = [r for r in csv.DictReader(open(f), delimiter='\\t') if r['Type']=='AMR']\n    g = sorted(set(r['Element symbol'] for r in rows))\n    def has(p): return [x for x in g if re.match(p, x)]\n    acq_bl = has(r'blaTEM|blaSHV|blaCTX-M|blaOXA|blaCMY|blaDHA|blaKPC|blaNDM|blaVIM|blaIMP|blaACC|blaFOX|blaMOX|blaACT|blaLAP|blaPSE|blaCARB')\n    esbl = [x for x in acq_bl if re.match(r'blaCTX-M|blaCMY|blaDHA|blaACC|blaFOX|blaMOX|blaACT|blaKPC|blaNDM|blaVIM|blaIMP|blaOXA-48|blaGES', x)]\n    esbl += [x for x in acq_bl if re.match(r'blaSHV|blaTEM', x) and any(r['Element symbol']==x and r['Subclass'] in ('CEPHALOSPORIN','CARBAPENEM') for r in rows)]\n    ampc_prom = has(r'ampC_')\n    carb = [x for x in g if any(r['Element symbol']==x and 'CARBAPENEM' in r['Subclass'] for r in rows)]\n    qrdr = has(r'gyrA_|parC_|parE_|gyrB_')\n    pmqr = has(r'qnr|aac\\(6\\'\\)-Ib-cr|qepA|oqxA|oqxB')\n    pmqr_strong = [x for x in pmqr if not x.startswith('oqx')]\n    gent = has(r'aac\\(3\\)|ant\\(2\\'\\'\\)|armA|rmt|npmA|aac\\(6\\'\\)-Ib-cr|aac\\(6\\'\\)-Ib$|aac\\(6\\'\\)-II')\n    gent = [x for x in gent if not x.startswith(\"aac(6')\")] or [x for x in gent]  # aac(6')-Ib -> tobramycin/amikacin; keep only if no other\n    gent = [x for x in gent if re.match(r'aac\\(3\\)|ant\\(2\\'\\'\\)|armA|rmt|npmA', x)]\n    dfr = has(r'dfr'); sul = has(r'sul[123]')\n    res = {}\n    res['ampicillin'] = ('R', '+'.join(acq_bl+ampc_prom)) if acq_bl or ampc_prom else ('S', 'no acquired beta-lactamase (chromosomal blaEC only)')\n    ce = esbl + ampc_prom\n    res['cefotaxime'] = ('R', '+'.join(ce)) if ce else ('S', 'no ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase' + ('; '+'+'.join(acq_bl)+' is narrow-spectrum' if acq_bl else ''))\n    res['meropenem'] = ('R', '+'.join(carb)) if carb else ('S', 'no carbapenemase found')\n    nq = len([x for x in qrdr if x.startswith(('gyrA','parC','parE'))])\n    if nq >= 2 or (nq >= 1 and pmqr_strong) or len(pmqr_strong) >= 2:\n        res['ciprofloxacin'] = ('R', '+'.join(qrdr+pmqr_strong))\n    elif nq == 1 or pmqr_strong:\n        res['ciprofloxacin'] = ('S', 'single determinant '+'+'.join(qrdr+pmqr_strong)+' (low-level, MIC usually <=0.25-0.5)')\n    else:\n        res['ciprofloxacin'] = ('S', 'no QRDR mutation or PMQR found')\n    res['gentamicin'] = ('R', '+'.join(gent)) if gent else ('S', 'no gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found')\n    if dfr:\n        res['trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole'] = ('R', '+'.join(dfr+sul))\n    else:\n        res['trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole'] = ('S', 'no dfr gene' + ('; '+'+'.join(sul)+' alone insufficient' if sul else ''))\n    for a in abx:\n        p, e = res.get(a, ('NA', 'antibiotic not covered by rules'))\n        out.write(f'{iso}\\t{a}\\t{p}\\t{e}\\n')\nEOF\npython3 -I scripts/call.py; cat output/predictions.tsv; wc -l output/predictions.tsv", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "isolate_id\tantibiotic\tprediction\tevidence\nISO_091\tampicillin\tR\tblaTEM-1\nISO_091\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase; blaTEM-1 is narrow-spectrum\nISO_091\tciprofloxacin\tS\tsingle determinant gyrA_S83L (low-level, MIC usually <=0.25-0.5)\nISO_091\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_091\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_091\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tR\tdfrA5+sul2\nISO_092\tampicillin\tS\tno acquired beta-lactamase (chromosomal blaEC only)\nISO_092\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\nISO_092\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_092\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_092\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_092\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene\nISO_093\tampicillin\tR\tblaTEM-1\nISO_093\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase; blaTEM-1 is narrow-spectrum\nISO_093\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_093\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_093\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_093\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tR\tdfrA5+sul2\nISO_094\tampicillin\tS\tno acquired beta-lactamase (chromosomal blaEC only)\nISO_094\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\nISO_094\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_094\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_094\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_094\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene\nISO_095\tampicillin\tR\tblaCTX-M-65\nISO_095\tcefotaxime\tR\tblaCTX-M-65\nISO_095\tciprofloxacin\tR\tgyrA_D87N+gyrA_S83L+parC_S80I\nISO_095\tgentamicin\tR\taac(3)-IVa\nISO_095\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_095\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene; sul1+sul2 alone insufficient\nISO_096\tampicillin\tR\tblaTEM-1\nISO_096\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase; blaTEM-1 is narrow-spectrum\nISO_096\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_096\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_096\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_096\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene; sul2 alone insufficient\nISO_097\tampicillin\tR\tblaCTX-M-14+blaTEM-1\nISO_097\tcefotaxime\tR\tblaCTX-M-14\nISO_097\tciprofloxacin\tR\tgyrA_D87N+gyrA_S83L+parC_A56T+parC_S80I\nISO_097\tgentamicin\tR\taac(3)-IVa\nISO_097\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_097\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tR\tdfrA12+sul2\nISO_098\tampicillin\tS\tno acquired beta-lactamase (chromosomal blaEC only)\nISO_098\tcefotaxime\tS\tno ESBL/AmpC/carbapenemase\nISO_098\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_098\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_098\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_098\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene\nISO_099\tampicillin\tR\tblaCTX-M-15\nISO_099\tcefotaxime\tR\tblaCTX-M-15\nISO_099\tciprofloxacin\tS\tsingle determinant gyrA_S83L (low-level, MIC usually <=0.25-0.5)\nISO_099\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_099\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_099\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tS\tno dfr gene\nISO_100\tampicillin\tR\tblaCTX-M-1\nISO_100\tcefotaxime\tR\tblaCTX-M-1\nISO_100\tciprofloxacin\tS\tno QRDR mutation or PMQR found\nISO_100\tgentamicin\tS\tno gentamicin-modifying enzyme/16S methylase found\nISO_100\tmeropenem\tS\tno carbapenemase found\nISO_100\ttrimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole\tR\tdfrA17+sul1+sul2\n      61 output/predictions.tsv", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01JMwXSKpwFUbLkvwUxkSAd2", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_010"}
{"cmd": "cd /Users/applemacbookpro/llm-amr-benchmark/runs/claude/rep1/batch_010/workspace; cat > output/methods.md <<'EOF'\n# Methods\n\n## Tools and databases\n- **AMRFinderPlus 4.2.7** (`amrfinder`), database version **2026-10-29.1** (local install; no update run, no network).\n  - Dependencies in the same conda env: BLAST+ 2.17.0, HMMER 3.4.\n- Python 3 (standard library only) for genotype-to-phenotype rules: `scripts/call.py`.\n- No other AMR tools were installed (abricate, RGI, ResFinder/PointFinder, staramr, mlst were checked and were absent).\n\n## Command\nFor each `data/genomes/ISO_###.fasta`:\n```\namrfinder -n ISO_###.fasta -O Escherichia --plus --threads 4 -o output/amrfinder/ISO_###.tsv\n```\n`-O Escherichia` turns on species-specific point-mutation screening (gyrA/parC/parE QRDR, ampC promoter, etc.). Default identity/coverage thresholds were used. Only rows with `Type == AMR` were used. Partial hits (PARTIALX / PARTIAL_CONTIG_ENDX) were kept, but none of them affected a call for the six antibiotics: they were aph(6)-Id, aph(4)-Ia and aadA5.\n\n## Genotype → S/R rules (`scripts/call.py`)\n- **Ampicillin**: R if any acquired beta-lactamase (blaTEM, blaSHV, blaCTX-M, blaOXA, plasmid AmpC, carbapenemases, …) or an ampC promoter/attenuator mutation is present. The chromosomal blaEC (including the blaEC-5 allele) on its own is not counted, so those isolates are called S.\n- **Cefotaxime**: R if an ESBL (CTX-M; TEM/SHV only when AMRFinder gives subclass CEPHALOSPORIN/CARBAPENEM), a plasmid AmpC (CMY, DHA, ACC, FOX, MOX, ACT), a carbapenemase or an ampC promoter mutation is present. Otherwise S. TEM-1 counts as narrow-spectrum.\n- **Meropenem**: R if any gene with AMRFinder subclass CARBAPENEM is present (carbapenemase). Otherwise S.\n- **Ciprofloxacin**: R if there are at least 2 QRDR mutations (gyrA/parC/parE), or at least 1 QRDR mutation plus a PMQR gene (qnr, aac(6')-Ib-cr, qepA), or at least 2 PMQR genes. A single gyrA mutation on its own (typical MIC 0.125–0.5 mg/L, around the S ≤0.25 breakpoint) is called S, and the evidence column flags it. oqxAB is not counted. marR_S3N is treated as a non-informative polymorphism.\n- **Gentamicin**: R if aac(3) (e.g. aac(3)-II/-IV/-VI), ant(2'')-Ia or a 16S rRNA methylase (armA, rmt*, npmA) is present. aph/aadA/aac(6')-Ib genes do not confer gentamicin resistance and are ignored.\n- **Trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole**: R if any dfrA/dfrB gene is present (it was always found together with sul1/2/3 here). A sul gene without dfr is called S, because trimethoprim resistance is needed for clinical SXT resistance.\n- No call was NA.\n\n## Limitations\n- Resistance from efflux overexpression, porin loss, or ampC hyperexpression that is not captured by the screened promoter mutations is not detected.\n- Calls near the breakpoint (single gyrA mutation) carry the most uncertainty. Gene copy number and expression level are not modelled.\nEOF\nls output", "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "amrfinder\nmethods.md\npredictions.tsv", "stderr": "", "tool": "bash", "source": "events.jsonl", "call_id": "toolu_01GSuiTXpRMCDkt3yvVYWiKw", "key_path": "message.content.0.input", "batch": "batch_010"}
